1
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:33,324
THE OHAGI OF DOOM

2
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:35,910
-<i>The Ohagi of Doom.</i>
-<i>The Ohagi of Doom.</i>

3
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:43,960
What? There's a ghost?

4
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:47,213
I've been standing in line
for three goddamn days…

5
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:51,301
just to enter the Rock-Paper-Scissors
Battle for a chance to buy one of ten,

6
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:54,721
'Ohagi Unicorns' from KYOTO,
the legendary Asian sweets shop…

7
00:00:54,804 --> 00:00:58,475
You think I've got time to waste
on a ghost?!

8
00:00:58,558 --> 00:00:59,934
Goodbye!

9
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:06,107
This is way too cute!
I could seriously watch it forever!

10
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:09,277
I need to have it! I need it! I need it!

11
00:01:10,195 --> 00:01:11,321
Now begins…

12
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:14,407
the Rock-Paper-Scissors Battle…

13
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:18,745
to win the right to purchase
the Ohagi Unicorn!

14
00:01:18,828 --> 00:01:22,582
-Challengers, are you prepared?
-Yeah!

15
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:25,502
Time to show the angel's power
of good luck.

16
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:27,504
Rock, paper,

17
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:30,131
scissors, go!

18
00:01:30,673 --> 00:01:33,968
Oh, my God! I'm the scissors master!

19
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,094
Fuck!

20
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:39,224
Oh, may the sweet rice ball be with us.

21
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:44,938
Yummy, yummy, yummy. I love mochi.

22
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:47,899
But I hate this bean paste.

23
00:01:49,317 --> 00:01:51,152
No!

24
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:54,739
Rock, paper, scissors.

25
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:57,242
Go! Go! Go!

26
00:01:57,325 --> 00:01:59,911
Go! Go!

27
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:01,454
Yahoo!

28
00:02:02,747 --> 00:02:06,626
Whether you like it or not, there's only
one ticket left for the Ohagi Unicorn.

29
00:02:06,709 --> 00:02:10,338
The final remaining contestant
will win the ticket!

30
00:02:10,421 --> 00:02:12,340
Let's do this… fair and square!

31
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:13,675
-Rock!
-Paper!

32
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:15,343
-Scissors!
-Go!

33
00:02:16,469 --> 00:02:17,679
Go!

34
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,681
Who are you?

35
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:22,016
I was born of the grudge
of the girl who died

36
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:25,395
from not getting to eat KYOTO's
limited-edition Ohagi last year.

37
00:02:25,478 --> 00:02:28,064
I am Okashi Daisuki Sato-Ichi.

38
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:30,316
Wow, Clone Wars!

39
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,568
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

40
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:35,321
How is she a clone of me?
I'm way cuter than her.

41
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:38,366
But if you're a ghost,
that makes things easier.

42
00:02:38,449 --> 00:02:39,617
Rock,

43
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:41,202
paper, scissors. Go!

44
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:45,290
-I am the 'Dual Wielding' Sato-Ni!
-I'm the 'Monohoshizao' Sato-San!

45
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:47,709
-Rock, paper, scissors.
-Rock, paper, scissors.

46
00:02:47,792 --> 00:02:48,918
-Go!
-Go!

47
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:57,886
I am the 'Lone Wolf and Cub' Sato-Yon!

48
00:02:58,511 --> 00:03:01,347
I am the 'Ninja' Sato-Go.

49
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:04,309
I am the 'Unfettered' Sato-Roku.

50
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:07,604
We are the 'Seven Satos' Sato-Nana!

51
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:10,857
-Rock, paper, scissors!
-Go!

52
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:12,442
Go!

53
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:13,568
Go!

54
00:03:13,651 --> 00:03:16,446
Go!

55
00:03:19,949 --> 00:03:23,912
Can you kill a kitty
with innocent eyes like me?

56
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:27,457
You're just some knockoff Honekoneko!

57
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,042
Help me. Meow.

58
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:31,628
It's cute!

59
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:34,005
Meow, meow, meow.

60
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:38,009
The younger Poly Peeps brother?

61
00:03:38,092 --> 00:03:40,386
You're going after the Ohagi Unicorn too?

62
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:42,513
What? Ohagi? What are you talking about?

63
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:44,974
Fighting ghosts is
an angel's routine duty.

64
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:47,560
-So you have allies.
-I'm doing what I should.

65
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:50,104
-If there's two of you, then…
-Don't step on me! Stop! Ow!

66
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:52,982
…watch this!

67
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:55,902
One hundred million

68
00:03:56,486 --> 00:03:58,821
ghosts!

69
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:02,784
I'm all about the easy Heaven Coins.

70
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:05,745
Lowkey super thankful for this.

71
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:11,876
Look at the time!
That's the end of my shift!

72
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:15,254
Switching to private time…
Peace! Great work today!

73
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:19,217
Why did you even come?

74
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,469
You good-for-nothing brat!

75
00:04:26,766 --> 00:04:29,727
Rock, paper, scissors!

76
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:33,022
Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

77
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:38,695
I can't kill one hundred million of them
with just two swords.

78
00:04:38,778 --> 00:04:41,239
Gunsmith Bitch!

79
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,949
Sell me a sword

80
00:04:43,032 --> 00:04:45,284
that can slay one hundred million ghosts!

81
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:48,454
Thanks for your business! Counterfeit,
irregular, watered down, and reinforced!

82
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:50,832
I'll name you a price!

83
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:55,920
{\an8}Super Shingan Stripe!

84
00:04:58,381 --> 00:05:01,884
I will never hand over
the last Ohagi Unicorn!

85
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:24,115
Killing one hundred million ghosts.
Accomplished!

86
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:27,076
This is the ticket

87
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:29,537
to buy an Ohagi Unicorn!

88
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:32,290
Finally! It's finally mine.

89
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:34,167
-Here, your bill.
-What?

90
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:38,004
The Heaven Coins from defeating those
one hundred million ghosts isn't enough.

91
00:05:38,087 --> 00:05:40,173
-Do you not have money?
-Nope.

92
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:42,008
Then I'll be taking this.

93
00:05:42,091 --> 00:05:44,218
My Ohagi Unicorn…

94
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:47,013
It's too sweet! Gross!

95
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:58,357
{\an8}NOT 2 HOME ALONE

96
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:00,902
{\an8}-<i>Not 2 Home alone.</i>
-<i>Not 2 Home alone.</i>

97
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:13,998
Looks like no one's home.

98
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:17,168
So, that means, like, you know,
our plan's working?

99
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:18,628
-Yay!
-Yay!

100
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:24,550
<i>I think there's a ghost over here.</i>

101
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:27,553
You keep saying "over here!" Over where?

102
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:29,555
<i>It's, like, over here?</i>

103
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:30,640
Oh, my god!

104
00:06:30,723 --> 00:06:33,267
Those assholes!
I don't care who or where!

105
00:06:33,351 --> 00:06:36,104
We're the ones takin'
down that damn ghost first!

106
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:42,819
I bet they're like, getting caught
in all our traps right now.

107
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:46,948
Like, our plan to distract them
and find their weaknesses

108
00:06:47,031 --> 00:06:50,660
to finally punish them
will be a huge success?

109
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:51,869
-Yay!
-Yay!

110
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:53,871
Okay. Let's split up the work.

111
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:55,873
And invade…

112
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:57,125
-…their rooms!
-…their rooms!

113
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:01,170
This is Panty's room?

114
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:03,923
She's like a total trash hoarder.

115
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:05,925
Click?

116
00:07:08,928 --> 00:07:10,179
What?

117
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,933
My clothes!

118
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:25,820
This… This feels dangerously unhinged.

119
00:07:25,903 --> 00:07:27,113
Nooo!

120
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:28,990
Panty, I'm coming in.

121
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:31,409
Wait! I didn't know the sisters
live with other people!

122
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:34,787
And like, I'm gonna get totally destroyed
by this contraption!

123
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:36,539
Stop, stop, wait, stop, stop, stop, stop!

124
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:48,509
P-Panty! You're using the fully automatic
sex machine again?!

125
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:53,431
<i>Wait. Has he not noticed,</i>
<i>or like,does he really think I'm Panty?</i>

126
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:57,476
<i>Does she always use this creepy device?</i>
<i>She's supposed to be an angel.</i>

127
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:00,479
S-So Panty, your back zipper…

128
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:01,564
You're right.

129
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:04,233
If-- if it's okay, I can do it!

130
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:06,402
But not because I wanna or anything weird!
I mean--I mean, I just wanna help!

131
00:08:06,485 --> 00:08:09,238
Thanks. You're Brief, right?
Can you get it then?

132
00:08:09,322 --> 00:08:11,616
<i>Serious!? She's letting me!?</i>

133
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:14,702
Wait? Brief?

134
00:08:14,785 --> 00:08:18,080
Wait, did Panty just call me Brief
instead of Geek Boy?

135
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:21,209
The Panty I know? Called me by my name?
This is way too suspicious!

136
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:23,127
Is this the real Panty standing
in front of me?

137
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:24,503
Are you out of your mind, Brief?

138
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:27,423
Stop yapping!
Behold the glory before your eyes!

139
00:08:27,506 --> 00:08:30,843
This is… the ultimate lovey-dovey
couple scenario I've dreamed of!

140
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:33,429
The girl goes, "Oh, no.
My hand won't reach. Zip me up?"

141
00:08:33,512 --> 00:08:35,765
Don't worry if it's the real Panty.

142
00:08:35,848 --> 00:08:39,227
Focus on zipping the dress
in front of you!

143
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,938
Focus!

144
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:45,733
<i>He really thinks I'm Panty.</i>

145
00:08:45,816 --> 00:08:46,901
<i>I know!</i>

146
00:08:46,984 --> 00:08:48,945
Do you know what my weakness is?

147
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:51,113
Fo… Fo…

148
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:53,366
Focus.

149
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:00,831
If I'm being

150
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:01,958
for real…

151
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:05,920
Stop, stop, stop, stop, stop.

152
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:07,755
Miss Stocking, are you home?

153
00:09:07,838 --> 00:09:09,090
What?

154
00:09:09,173 --> 00:09:12,301
I didn't know the sisters lived
with anyone!

155
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:15,972
I'm, like, definitely done for!

156
00:09:16,055 --> 00:09:19,141
I've made Hell's special
black mandrake tea.

157
00:09:19,225 --> 00:09:21,852
Oh, my. Miss Stocking.

158
00:09:21,936 --> 00:09:25,022
You've been binging on sweets again,
haven't you? Just look at that face!

159
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:27,608
And what's with
the ridiculous contraption?

160
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:29,193
Why are there demons?

161
00:09:29,443 --> 00:09:32,071
<i>Wait. Maybe they don't realize who I am.</i>

162
00:09:32,154 --> 00:09:35,992
Have you forgotten that we've been
living together for the past six months?

163
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:39,537
Sister, expecting that level of memory
from an angel is rather optimistic.

164
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,372
That's true.

165
00:09:41,455 --> 00:09:43,541
Get out of my face, annoying demons.

166
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:46,377
<i>Oh wait… I can use them to get information</i>

167
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:48,796
<i>about Stocking's weakness.</i>

168
00:09:48,879 --> 00:09:51,257
Excuse me? How rude.

169
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:54,218
Demon, tell me my weakness.

170
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:56,721
What? Your weakness? It's that--

171
00:09:56,804 --> 00:09:58,347
Do not speak, demon.

172
00:09:58,431 --> 00:10:00,683
No! Speak, demon!

173
00:10:02,476 --> 00:10:06,856
-The other day, your least favorite--
-No, shut it, demon! No, don't shut it!

174
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:09,108
Hurry up and tell me!

175
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:13,571
<i>It's time for dinner!</i>

176
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:17,241
Man, I'm totally starving…

177
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:19,035
What's for dinner tonight?

178
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:22,288
It's Wednesday, so I'm guessing meat?

179
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:26,000
-What's with your outfit?
-You too.

180
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:28,377
Panty, Stocking. What are you doing?

181
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:31,464
Today is Garter's special big black
frankfurter burgers!

182
00:10:31,547 --> 00:10:34,383
What's the matter? You're usually greedily
the first to devour them.

183
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:36,010
Indeed. Just as Sister says.

184
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:39,263
I think I might be hungry.

185
00:10:39,347 --> 00:10:42,683
But wait! I don't want to eat with demons!

186
00:10:45,603 --> 00:10:48,356
Hey! You damn angels! Dinner's
gettin' cold! Move your asses, now!

187
00:10:49,982 --> 00:10:51,275
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

188
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:53,235
We're off angel duty!

189
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:56,697
Wow, the big black frankfurter
burger looks delicious.

190
00:10:56,781 --> 00:10:59,241
Why did we come again?

191
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:02,244
Like, who cares?

192
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:03,996
You're right.

193
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,123
-Thank you for the meal!
-Thank you for the meal!

194
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:07,875
-<i>Over here!</i>
-<i>Over here!</i>

195
00:11:07,958 --> 00:11:10,961
Fuck! Which way is 'over here,' huh!?

196
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:13,589
I know! "Over here" means that way!

197
00:11:13,672 --> 00:11:15,966
Okay, that way! Let's go, Stocking!

198
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:17,051
Yeah!

199
00:11:21,555 --> 00:11:26,644
{\an8}-<i>Six hundred Sixty Six Candles.</i>
-<i>Six hundred Sixty Six Candles.</i>

200
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:32,441
It's ready.

201
00:11:33,609 --> 00:11:34,693
Open your eyes,

202
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:37,279
Dearest Kneesocks.

203
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:39,365
Wow.

204
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:41,826
A big cake!

205
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:44,036
Of course!

206
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:47,081
It's your sixth birthday!

207
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:49,625
Any demon knows, a birthday ending in six…

208
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:52,670
demand most fabulous celebration.
It's simply the rule!

209
00:11:52,753 --> 00:11:55,005
Now hurry up.

210
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:57,466
And one more thing.

211
00:11:57,550 --> 00:12:02,430
When you blow, make a wish,
and blow them out in one breath.

212
00:12:02,513 --> 00:12:05,599
That's the rule!

213
00:12:05,683 --> 00:12:06,892
Now, hurry, hurry!

214
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:15,067
Happy birthday, Kneesocks!

215
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:19,071
Wow! Thank you, Scanty!

216
00:12:21,907 --> 00:12:23,909
What beautiful glasses.

217
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:29,874
-What do you think?
-Wow!

218
00:12:30,624 --> 00:12:33,961
I can see your beautiful face clearly!

219
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:35,963
My my, Kneesocks.

220
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:40,509
So what did you wish for?

221
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:42,219
Um…

222
00:12:43,095 --> 00:12:45,473
I wished to spend all my birthdays

223
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:48,642
with my beloved sister!

224
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,019
Dear me.

225
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:53,272
Then I shall grant your wish!

226
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:55,774
-Really?
-Of course!

227
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:58,235
Granting my cute little sister's wish!

228
00:12:58,319 --> 00:13:01,071
That is my responsibility
as your older sister!

229
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:03,908
I swear to celebrate

230
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:06,076
every birthday with you,

231
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,745
no matter what.

232
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:12,625
Listen, Kneesocks.

233
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:15,878
Just between the two of us Demon sisters,

234
00:13:15,961 --> 00:13:17,963
this is our rule.

235
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:24,178
<i>Dearest Sister… You liar.</i>

236
00:13:25,304 --> 00:13:26,722
<i>Currently, in this early morning,</i>

237
00:13:26,805 --> 00:13:31,685
<i>the ghost on Rodeo Street in western</i>
<i>Daten City escaped to the neighborhoods.</i>

238
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:34,855
<i>Schools and residents in the</i>
<i>surrounding area should be on high alert.</i>

239
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:37,691
<i>Angels who let the ghost escape are</i>
<i>questioned on their responsi--</i>

240
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:38,984
Shut up!

241
00:13:42,029 --> 00:13:45,824
Had myself a breakfast fuck,
now I'm starving.

242
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:47,535
Hey, Garter! Breakfast!

243
00:13:48,702 --> 00:13:50,704
Stocking! Chuck!

244
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,122
Geek Boy!

245
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:54,291
Fuck. Is no one here?

246
00:13:54,375 --> 00:13:56,752
-Hey, Scanty! Kneeso--
-Not here.

247
00:13:57,711 --> 00:14:00,673
Whoa! Say something if you're here!

248
00:14:00,756 --> 00:14:02,341
She's not here.

249
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:06,262
I can't hear what you're saying.

250
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:08,806
